# Generated by MATLAB, per-machine, and regenerated on every run.
# Git's own content addressing is the integrity mechanism here; the
# manifest exists for the Tier-B chat handoff, where there is no git.
MANIFEST.txt

# MATLAB
*.asv
*.autosave
*.mex*
slprj/
codegen/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Build outputs
#
# docs/html IS TRACKED, and that is a consequence of D-020. While the
# .mltbx shipped the built pages, ignoring them was right: they were an
# archive artefact, rebuilt on every release. Distribution is git now, so
# a clone IS the delivery - and an ignored manual means a user clones the
# toolbox, runs `doc geoMap`, and info.xml points help_location at a
# folder that does not exist (PV-146).
#
# The discipline that keeps a checked-in build honest already exists:
# geoMapAudit's documentationSync hashes every help block against the
# page built from it and fails the gate when they part. That check has
# been running since Stage F.2; it is what caught the five stale pages
# this round.
*.mltbx
test-results/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
